From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael S. Tsirkin" <mst@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:11:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vhost: split out-of-order used ring batches at every wrap

When a completion batch larger than the remaining space in the used
ring is added without VIRTIO_F_IN_ORDER, vhost_add_used_n_ooo() splits
it at the ring boundary only once. vhost-net can batch up to
VHOST_NET_BATCH TX completions, so with a queue smaller than half the
batch the tail of the second chunk runs past the end of the used ring
and into whatever follows it in the vhost owner's address space: with
a 32 entry queue, last_used_idx % 32 == 3 and a 64 entry batch, three
used entries are written past the ring.

To fix, keep splitting the remaining batch at each wrap until it is
exhausted.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Seohyeon Maeng <bioloidgp@gmail.com>
Cc: minki@morningstarsec.dev
Fixes: 2b3b35eb989 ("vhost_net: batch used ring update in rx")
Fixes: 4afb52c2af44 ("vhost_net: batch update used ring for datacopy TX")
Cc: Jason Wang <jasowangio@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Michael S. Tsirkin <mst@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5570a998b884c988dbe105430d7e2d8e9411e37e)
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 drivers/vhost/vhost.c | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/vhost/vhost.c b/drivers/vhost/vhost.c
index 6e72e72c3a178f3f313c895914037a29d91cb6cf..622d1e858f2f70afbf2df519b6fe63d0044be999 100644
--- a/drivers/vhost/vhost.c
+++ b/drivers/vhost/vhost.c
@@ -3104,18 +3104,21 @@ static int vhost_add_used_n_ooo(struct vhost_virtqueue *vq,
 				struct vring_used_elem *heads,
 				unsigned count)
 {
-	int start, n, r;
+	unsigned int n;
+	int r;
 
-	start = vq->last_used_idx & (vq->num - 1);
-	n = vq->num - start;
-	if (n < count) {
+	do {
+		unsigned int start = vq->last_used_idx & (vq->num - 1);
+
+		n = min(vq->num - start, count);
 		r = __vhost_add_used_n(vq, heads, n);
 		if (r < 0)
 			return r;
 		heads += n;
 		count -= n;
-	}
-	return __vhost_add_used_n(vq, heads, count);
+	} while (count);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int vhost_add_used_n_in_order(struct vhost_virtqueue *vq,
